description:
QUICKSTART.md's "Reproduce the benchmark" section tells the user to run:

    uv run mathgraph bench

and says "Expected, on the held-out PFR blueprint:" followed by (lines 104-105):

    {"lexical":     {"n": 175, "recall@1": 0.189, "recall@5": 0.32},
     "+structural": {"n": 175, "recall@1": 0.2,   "recall@5": 0.389}}

I ran the exact command shown: `MATHGRAPH_DATA=/workspace/mathgraph-data uv run mathgraph bench`. Actual current output:

    {
      "lexical": {"n": 176, "recall@1": 0.182, "recall@5": 0.318},
      "+structural": {"n": 176, "recall@1": 0.193, "recall@5": 0.381}
    }

The documented block is not a rounding difference -- it is exactly the OLD pre-scanner-fix numbers (compare to README.md:930-933's table explicitly labeled "n=175, pre-scanner-fix corpus": 18.9/32.0 lexical, 20.0/38.9 structural -- same values as QUICKSTART's 0.189/0.32/0.2/0.389). QUICKSTART never labels its block as historical; it reads as "this is what you should see when you run the command right now," and the very next paragraph (108-111) already anticipates drift ("If those numbers don't reproduce exactly, the corpora have moved on..."), which argues for keeping this block current rather than freezing it.

Fix: replace the JSON block at QUICKSTART.md:104-105 with the current measured output above (n=176, lexical 0.182/0.318, structural 0.193/0.381), matching README.md:937's already-current "18.2 / 31.8 and 19.3 / 38.1" figures (which are correct and need no change -- confirmed by the same command).

Evidence that closes this: re-run `MATHGRAPH_DATA=/workspace/mathgraph-data uv run mathgraph bench` and diff its stdout against the updated QUICKSTART block.
